      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "परं यस्याः । with an eye solely to wealth; greedy. वदान्य–liberal,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "munificent. नित्य may be taken either as adj. or adv. in the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "dissolution of the compounds, नित्यव्यया and प्रचुरनित्यधनागमा. The",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "fig. is उपमा.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 48. आज्ञा—power to enforce command. Râmrshi con-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "siders the word ब्राह्मणानाम् to be an उपलक्षण i. e. as in-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "cluding all people. The Brâhmaṇas are specially mentioned as",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "most deserving help and protection, their priestly avocation",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "making it impossible for them to defend themselves with arms",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "&c. येषां एते &c. who have not gained these six qualities (special",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "advantages ). पार्थिवोपाश्रय—taking shelter with a king i. e.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "becoming royal servants or favourites. Or पार्थिव may be taken",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "as Voc. singular; in this case तेषां may refere to kings; what is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "the use of resorting to those kings who do not &c.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 49. मरुस्थले—मरु is the waterless tract now known as",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "Mârwâr. म्रियन्तेऽस्मिन् भूतानि जलाभावात् इति मरुः, fr. मृ + उ Un. I. 7.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "मेरौ—on the mountain Meru, the store-house of wealth. Accord-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "ing to the Purânas the mountain Meru is formed of gold and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "jewels. It is the loftiest mountain on earth and the centre",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "round which the whole firmament revolves. कृपणां वृत्तिं मा कृथाः—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "do not act or behave in an abject manner. The last line shows",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "that on the capacity of a man depends his fortune, and it should",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "be rightly understood to counteract the effect of the first which",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "is fatalistic. The fig. is दृष्टान्त. See sl. 57.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "Sl. 50. गोचर—moving within the range of the senses ( गो );",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "hence, known. See supra sl. 16. कार्पण्योक्तिः—words expressive",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "of our pitiful condition, supplication. The fig. here is अप्रस्तुतप्रशं-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "सा. Some liberal person is addressed with these words which",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "apparently refer to the cloud. अप्रस्तुतप्रशंसा is thus defined:—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "अप्रस्तुतप्रशंसा सा या सैव प्रस्तुताश्रया K. P. X.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 51. सावधानमनसा—with close or assiduous attention.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "एतादृशाः—such, referring to चातकाधार in the above S'loka. Al-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "though the slokas are not much connected with each other still",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
